INT. CLOSED FUNICULAR STATION - CAR HOUSE - DAY

A dusty hillside funicular terminal. Two wooden cars rest on rails that slope up into a tunnel. Sunlight drips through slatted windows. A card table is set up between the cars, covered in blueprints, a thermos, and a plate of lemon biscuits.

FELIX "THE CLOCK" BRANDTNER (60s, vest, pocket watch) pours tea. BIANCA MORETTI (30s, tool belt, calm eyes) sketches on a napkin. Big DESMOND "DEZ" OKONKWO (40s, forearms like cables) polishes a wrench. Young TOBIAS PIKE (20s, nervous, tall) clutches a thermos. And RENATA "RENNY" SILVA (50s, reading glasses, ledger) turns pages.

                    FELIX
          Biscuit, Bianca?

                    BIANCA
          Not now, Felix. The cable tension is wrong.

                    DEZ
          It's been wrong since 1962, Bee.

                    RENNY
          And the vault is exactly where it's been since 1962, Dez.

                    TOBIAS
          Is it, though? I looked at the survey and the vault is on the--

                    FELIX
          Tobias, my boy, finish your tea.

                    TOBIAS
          I'm just saying, Clock, the survey shows--

                    BIANCA
          --the east wall, Toby, I know. I drew it.

                    DEZ
          So we go up the east wall.

                    RENNY
          We go up Thursday. Nobody does anything today.

                    FELIX
          Splendid. Renny, you keep the ledger.

                    RENNY
          I always keep the ledger, Felix.

                    DEZ
          Bee, pass me the biscuits.

                    BIANCA
          Dez, you have a wrench in your hand.

                    DEZ
          I have two hands.

Tobias, finally, takes a biscuit. Everyone watches him chew. He nods.

                    TOBIAS
          Thursday.

                    FELIX
          Thursday.
